{"id":"u-609ac046-7614-411b-a92a-7b175fce51fe","src":"community","title":"Modified GBR Rest-Pause U/L: I've Got Shit To Do","author":"Posture King","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/wSNyXN-upperlowerprogram","desc":"A loosely bastardised version of Lyle McDonald’s GBR, inspired by the discussions in Lyle’s Facebook group, but done entirely with rest-pause / DC-style sets.\n\nOne hard set. ~15 seconds of rest (or 15 breaths). Go again until the reps get shit. That’s it. No fucking faff.\n\nI’m nearly 30, work a shitty IT job, and my body is slowly falling apart, so I don’t have the time or inclination to spend two hours in the gym pretending every set needs a fucking spreadsheet. Miss a day? Have a lie-in? Life gets in the way? Who gives a shit. Train when you can, recover, and get back at it.\n\nWorks for bulking, cutting, recomping and RFL. Train hard, recover properly, eat enough protein, and stop looking for magical fucking optimisation nobody needs.\n\nLow volume. High effort. Short sessions. Legs are usually ~15–20 minutes. Upper ~40–50, depending on how much I’m fucking about, how busy the gym is, or whether someone is using the cable machine for an exercise that could’ve been done with literally anything else.\n\nBasically, bodybuilding for people with jobs, responsibilities, questionable sleep schedules and joints that make noises they definitely didn’t used to make.\n\nYou don’t need more exercises. You don’t need more volume. You probably don’t need another fucking programme.\n\nThis shit works. Do it.\n\nAnd yes, Lyle was right.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-07T14:20:17.507Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10}]},{"n":"Kelso Shrug (Chest Supported)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10}]},{"n":"Incl